#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""BMeet - dictation, meeting transcripts and file transcripts in one window.

Usage:
  bmeet [meetings|files|transcribe] [--id MEETING_ID] [--file PATH]... [FILE...]
  bmeet --version

  meetings|files|transcribe   page to show (default: the page used last)
  --id ID                     select this meeting (voxtype meeting id)
  --file PATH, FILE           an audio/video file is queued on "Transcribe a file";
                              a transcript (.md/.srt/.txt) from the list or a meeting's
                              Markdown copy is selected on its page

One window per user: a second launch hands its arguments to the running window
(local socket in $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR) and raises it.

A front end for voxtype (dictation daemon + meetings on the Intel NPU) and
npu-transcribe (Whisper on the NPU for audio/video files). Live state comes from
bmeet-ctl (imported, not spawned); meetings are read from voxtype's SQLite
index (read-only); exports and deletes go through voxtype's CLI. Runs on the
system PyQt6, so it gets the Breeze style and the KDE file dialogs.

Environment (testing): BMEET_CTL, BMEET_VOXTYPE, BMEET_TRANSCRIBE,
BMEET_SOCKET, BMEET_DEBUG=1, BMEET_DRY_RUN=1 (log instead of
recording, starting meetings, switching language, opening files/folders,
notifying), plus bmeet-ctl's BMEET_MEETING_DB, BMEET_RUN_DIR,
VOXTYPE_MEETING_DIR and NPU_TRANSCRIBE_HISTORY.

On macOS the same window runs inside BMeet.app (Contents/Helpers/BMeet Window.app, on BMeet's
venv PyQt6): BMeet.app dictates and macos/bmeet-meeting records meetings, so its actions go
through bmeet-ctl to BMeet.app, and exports and deletes through bmeet-meeting.
"""
